  "disclosures": [
    "The injection PHENOMENON (a finite-budget contact sweep depositing energy) is known prior art and is conceded, not claimed. What the two arms differ in is the contact-row modal weight.",
    "Both arms are independent runs from identical build states; nothing is toggled mid-trajectory and no body is parked or isolated.",
    "The passivity governor / clamp is OFF in both arms. The fixed arm's boundedness comes from the row weight alone.",
    "The boundary is an energy-SIGN effect, not a stability threshold: the unfixed arm never goes non-finite over this clip.",
    "The unfixed arm is already +0.1 J from the fixed arm at the instant the pot lands: the RESTING objects' own support rows inject during the fall.",
    "D2: the headline joules are almost entirely table-MODE (modal) energy, not the objects' own motion. At the unfixed peak: E_total = 857 J, of which E_modal = 843.1 J (98.386%), while the bodies' translational KE is 4.509 J (bystanders alone 0.005398 J).",
    "Fidelity caveat: the matched weight is CONSERVATIVE here. Against the substep-matched converged reference the fixed arm under-moves the bystanders (7.6 mm vs 11.8 mm peak rise, 3.6 deg vs 4.5 deg peak tilt) while the unfixed arm over-moves them by 2.8x.",
    "The two converged self-references AGREE to within 1.7% on the legitimate bystander scale (11.78 mm at the recorded substep grid vs 11.58 mm at one substep per frame), so 'the true motion' is quoted as the range 11.58-11.78 mm, never as a single number.",
    "Both arms still show a spurious impactor rebound (22.4 mm unfixed, 5.1 mm fixed, 9.5 mm converged): the matched weight fixes the modal contact row, not every fixed-budget error.",
    "The render draw order (support behind bodies) was checked with the video's own render3d.assert_layering_valid on sampled frames of every recorded arm: unfixed OK (worst slack -1.382 mm); fixed OK (worst slack -0.571 mm); ref OK (worst slack -1.018 mm).",
    "D1: the effect is BUDGET-GRADED, not a property of the scene. Holding the substep grid fixed and raising only the iteration count, the same shipped weight gives 1x8 -> +808.8 J; 2x8 -> +3.162 J; 4x8 -> +0 J; 8x8 -> +0 J. The recorded operating point (1 iteration(s) x 8 substeps) must therefore be stated wherever these numbers are shown.",
    "No real-time claim is supported by this recording: it is an offline CPU float64 run."
